course: dictionary
lesson: 12337
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Coverage is one of them. Read the words around it to find the meaning that fits. «The football fans watched live coverage of the final on TV.» Here coverage means the reporting of an event as it happens.
explain: «The sun cream has good coverage, so your arms are safe.» Here coverage means how much of your skin the cream covers. The clue is the cream on your skin, not the news.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could you say "live reporting of the final"? Yes, so the meaning fits. Coverage can also mean how fully a topic is included, as in «The book has good coverage of the planets», which means it includes a lot about them.
fact: Coverage is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say "good coverage", not "a coverage".
fact: Coverage can mean the reporting of news or events on TV, radio, in newspapers or online.
fact: Coverage can mean how much of an area or surface is covered by something, like phone signal or paint.
fact: In insurance, coverage means what a policy will pay for, such as theft.
fact: Coverage can also mean how fully a topic or set of things is included. Common phrases: live coverage, phone coverage, full coverage.
exercise: «The match had live coverage on TV.» What does coverage mean here? | Paint spread over a wall | *The reporting of the match as it happens | A small ticket to the game | A soft blanket for a bed
exercise: «Our phone has no coverage in the valley.» What does coverage mean? | A type of blanket | Lots of rain | The price of a new phone | *Whether a phone signal reaches the place
exercise: «The insurance gives coverage for theft.» What does coverage mean? | *What the insurance will pay for | A holiday trip | Who wrote the insurance | How long the shop is open
test: «The book has good coverage of the planets.» What does coverage mean? | The book has been read by many people | The book is very heavy | *The book includes a lot about the planets
test: «The newspaper's coverage of the flood was clear and fair.» What does coverage mean? | A cover for the newspaper | The price of the newspaper | *The news reporting of the flood | A map of the river
exam: Jayden reads, «The paint has poor coverage, so the wall needs three coats.» What does coverage mean? | *How much of the wall the paint covers | The price of the paint | How long the paint takes to dry | The colour of the wall
